  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_1 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E] [inst_2 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E] [SecondCountableTopology E] (eta : ℝ),\n  0 < eta →\n    ∀ (h : E),\n      √eta ^ 2 = eta ∧\n        (Measurable fun q =>\n            (q.1.1 + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * q.1.2) • (q.2.1 - q.1.1) + Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * q.1.2) • q.2.2,\n              (Real.pi / 2) •\n                (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * q.1.2) • (q.2.1 - q.1.1) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * q.1.2) • q.2.2))) ∧\n          (∀ (r : ℝ),\n              MeasureTheory.Measure.map\n                  (fun p =>\n                    (h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * r) • (p.1 - h) + Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * r) • p.2,\n                      (Real.pi / 2) • (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * r) • (p.1 - h) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * r) • p.2)))\n                  ((MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun x => h + √eta • x) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)).prod\n                    (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => √eta • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))) =\n                (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun x => h + √eta • x) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)).prod\n                  (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => (Real.pi / 2 * √eta) • z) (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))) ∧\n            (∀ (p : E × E) (r : ℝ),\n                HasDerivAt (fun t => h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * t) • (p.1 - h) + Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * t) • p.2)\n                  ((Real.pi / 2) • (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * r) • (p.1 - h) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * r) • p.2)) r) ∧\n              ∀ (p : E × E),\n                h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * 0) • (p.1 - h) + Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * 0) • p.2 = h + p.2 ∧\n                  h + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * 1) • (p.1 - h) + Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * 1) • p.2 = p.1 ∧\n                    (Real.pi / 2) • (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * 0) • (p.1 - h) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * 0) • p.2) =\n                        (Real.pi / 2) • (p.1 - h) ∧\n                      (Real.pi / 2) • (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * 1) • (p.1 - h) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * 1) • p.2) =\n                        -(Real.pi / 2) • p.2",
    "statement_sha256": "ff8ba7804e5e560df9822bfaf007945ca6f136e6194bda77ecf86acf80c02c2f",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "stdGaussian E is the probability law of a centered isotropic Gaussian vector with identity covariance on the finite-dimensional real inner product space E.",
      "Measure.map f mu is the actual pushforward of mu by f, and Measure.prod is the independent product measure. A scaled or translated standard Gaussian is defined by the displayed map, not by an extra distributional assumption.",
      "The measurable function quantified before the timewise law has input type (E times Real) times (E times E). Its projections q.1.1,q.1.2,q.2.1,q.2.2 are center, time, first vector and second vector.",
      "HasDerivAt f v r means the real-parameter vector-valued function f has derivative v at r. Scalar multiplication is real scalar multiplication; Real.sqrt is the nonnegative square root.",
      "All local semantic definitions were expanded from the compiled theorem type and Lean verified definitional equality."
